<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_SandCatches.xml                      RimMandrake — STILLSAND_BEDAZZLE_CONTENT_1 (Q11a tier move)

  The item half of the sand-swimmer family, moved here from SWBestiary: the catch
  (RM_DuneCrawler, was RSW_DuneCrawler) and the rare prize (RM_GlassPearl, was
  RSW_GlassPearl). Both are invented, so they belong in the franchise-free RM
  tier. RSW_SandStalker, the predator that catches the catcher, stays RSW until
  the owner rules otherwise. The fishing hookup itself (fishTypes on RM_Stillsand)
  is STILLSAND_SAND_SWIM_KIT_1's job; the references in other mods were repointed.

  NEVER FISH-SHAPED (owner's explicit instruction): both are armored/crystalline
  analogs, not fish. ANTI-EXPONENTIAL: Nutrition/MarketValue stay at or below the
  vanilla Fish_* tier; the thin-windfall cap lives on the biome side.

  ART: both icons are PLACEHOLDERS (the old SWBestiary egg and trophy icons, copied
  into this mod's own Textures/Things/Item/Resource). Real art is queued in
  infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/stillsand_content_fill.csv (RM_DuneCrawler,
  RM_GlassPearl).
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="FishBase">
    <defName>RM_DuneCrawler</defName>
    <label>dune crawler</label>
    <description>A fist-sized, many-legged scavenger with a fused mineral shell, pulled up out of deep sand on a fishing line. It spends its whole life below the surface filtering decayed organics out of the sand — silverbole leaf-fall, dead things the dune swallowed, whatever a wreck sheds — and only ever reaches the light when something eats it or something catches it. Nothing about it says "fish." Cooked, it eats like a shrimp with regrets.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RM_DuneCrawler</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <!-- LONGSHADE_SHEET_STRUCTURAL_RULINGS_1 (owner 2026-10-04, Stillsand sheet: "Make this 1/3 size"): drawSize 1 (default) -> 0.33. -->
      <drawSize>0.33</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RM_GlassPearl</defName>
    <label>glass pearl</label>
    <description>A smooth, water-clear nodule fused out of silica deep inside a deep-sand pool — kin to the light-pipe nubs that dot the dune sea's surface, but rounder, and rarer, because nothing usually digs this deep to find one. Desert-world optics traders call a good one "a lens that grew a skin." Sold whole, or cut for what's inside.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RM_GlassPearl</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>38</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.15</Mass>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Beauty>4</Beauty>
      <DeteriorationRate>1</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <alwaysHaulable>true</alwaysHaulable>
    <stackLimit>25</stackLimit>
    <tradeability>Sellable</tradeability>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>ExoticMisc</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
